WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.590
The saga is ending, but will the story live
on forever?

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:07.790
On December 16, the ninth Star Wars film and
the final installment of the Skywalker saga

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.460
The Rise of Skywalker had its world premiere
in Los Angeles.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.840
Critics took to social media following the
event to share their thoughts about the film.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:18.200
We hesitate to say that there's a general
consensus about The Rise of Skywalker at this

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.980
point, since full reviews have yet to be posted
online and because critics are barred from

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.950
revealing too much in their early reactions.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.590
What we can say, however, is that there have
been more positive reactions to the film than

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.480
negative ones, with a common thread in critics'
tweets being that The Rise of Skywalker is

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.980
a larger-than-life, better-than-expected conclusion
to the 40-plus-year-long Skywalker saga.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.000
Fandango's Erik Davis held nothing back.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:38.720
He tweeted:

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.220
"Epic.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:39.900
All of it.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.520
[The film] is a terrific finale that is just
stuffed with so much of everything.

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:47.359
Action, adventure — answers!! — humor,
heart, love, and grit.

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:50.910
I spent the entire second half with tears
in my eyes – a wonderful way to end the

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.020
Skywalker story."

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.720
Entertainment journalist Jenna Busch was moved
to tears during the premiere of The Rise of

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.229
Skywalker, as it checked every box and delivered
on every promise.

00:00:59.229 --> 00:00:59.720
She tweeted:

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.600
"OH MY GOD!

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.220
I am absolutely blown away!

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.200
I've never been so satisfied by a film.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.040
This is the end of an era and a franchise
that has defined my life and this did it justice

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.640
in a way I didn't imagine it could.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:10.740
You WILL cry."

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.870
Shortly after seeing The Rise of Skywalker
on Monday evening, Slashfilm founder Peter

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:15.800
Sciretta tweeted:

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.960
"JJ Abrams nailed it.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.480
He was able to bring a cohesive arc to this
trilogy that feels like a fitting end to the

00:01:20.491 --> 00:01:21.491
saga as a whole.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.060
I'm so emotionally drained.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.760
Star Wars fans will be very happy."

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.100
It appears that one way The Rise of Skywalker
accomplishes the lofty goal of ending the

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.120
Skywalker saga with a bold bang is through
fan service, which critics have conflicting

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:33.840
emotions about.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.740
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.290
The official Twitter account for CinemaBlend
tweeted that The Rise of Skywalker is, quote,

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.840
"jammed with fan service" — but the kind
that will probably divide fans and spark heated

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.820
discussions about the Star Wars universe.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.620
Film and television critic Yolanda Machado
shared that she wasn't entirely surprised

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.980
by the events of The Rise of Skywalker, and
felt that, quote, "too much fan service was

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:53.480
given."

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.000
However, those downsides didn't detract from
the overall greatness of what The Rise of

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.250
Skywalker does and accomplishes in her eyes.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.770
Machado tweeted that the film is, quote, "everything
and nothing that you're expecting."

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.770
She went on to say:

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.430
"God I love this franchise and I'll miss the
Skywalker saga."

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.469
Award-winning journalist and film critic Scott
Mantz had similar feelings about the fan service

00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:14.180
in The Rise of Skywalker: there's a lot of
it, but he really enjoyed the film as a whole.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.240
He made no mention of what the result of packing
so much fan service into the film might be,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.400
though, instead keeping his reaction contained
to his own excited thoughts.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.000
He tweeted:

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.260
"Really awesome!

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.560
The best of the new trilogy!

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.360
Really fun, lots of humor, a big heart!

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.560
So many surprises!

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.060
It's everything #StarWars fans are hoping
for, and more!

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.880
A very satisfying conclusion!

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.820
A lot of fan service, but I loved it!"

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.260
You know the old saying: too much of a good
thing is a bad thing.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.320
For some critics, this adage applies to The
Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.239
Mashable's Chris Taylor kept his feelings
about The Rise of Skywalker short and simple,

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.620
unlike what he felt the movie was.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.200
He wrote:

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.680
"#TheRiseofSkywalker is a lot.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.580
It's like 9 movies of plot in one.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.600
Going to take me about 9 days to process."

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:56.180
Angie J. Han, also of Mashable, echoed Taylor's
sentiments in tweeting that The Rise of Skywalker

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:56.840
is "a lot."

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.219
She expanded, quote, "Tons to love here, no
shortage of crowd pleasing moments and twists

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.320
and cameos, but also quite a bit to [think
about]."

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.780
Han also hinted at an emotionally fulfilling
send-off for Carrie Fisher's Leia Organa,

00:03:07.799 --> 00:03:12.249
and some heart-warming moments with new characters
Jannah and D-0, a little droid pal who looks

00:03:12.249 --> 00:03:13.849
like he has a megaphone for a head.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:17.519
Collider editor-in-chief Steven Weintraub
was particularly cryptic in his reaction to

00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:21.290
The Rise of Skywalker, but what he did offer
following the premiere of the film suggests

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.640
that he may not have enjoyed it.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.020
On Monday night, he tweeted:

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.820
"I might be in the minority on #TheRiseofSkywalker.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.279
I have a lot to say but will wait till after
it has opened."

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.379
"I have a bad feeling about this."

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.720
OK, OK, you guys… we get it!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.500
It goes without saying that these are but
a selection of the many first reactions to

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.180
The Rise of Skywalker that critics were able
to put out on social media without getting

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.049
into hot water with the legal departments
at Disney and Lucasfilm.

00:03:44.049 --> 00:03:47.819
Far more in-depth reviews of the film will
be available to read once the companies lift

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:53.099
the review embargo for The Rise of Skywalker
on Wednesday, December 18 at 12:01am ET — a

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.580
full day before Thursday-night previews begin
on December 19.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.820
As the world witnessed in 2017 with The Last
Jedi, everyone is going to have their own

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:03.680
unique opinion about The Rise of Skywalker,
and there could be a big divide between critics

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.300
and fans once the flick officially launches
in theaters.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.240
While absorbing other people's reactions to
a movie is generally a harmless, hype-boosting

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.029
activity in the lead-up to the premiere, it's
important to remember that just because millions

00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:17.920
of people love the same property you do, it
doesn't mean you'll see eye to eye with them.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.030
That said, it's best to head into your Rise
of Skywalker screenings this week with an

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.940
open mind that's prepared for anything and
everything to happen.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.020
You may love it, or you may hate it, but the
only way to find out is to see The Rise of

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.280
Skywalker yourself on Thursday, December 19.

